# Grace interaction smoke: exercise the Motif menu popup path and the canvas
# rubber-band feedback under libx11-compat. Loads the fixture, opens the File
# menu (popup must map and render), dismisses it with Escape, then drags a
# zoom rubber-band across the plot canvas. The canvas must stay visible and the
# process must stay alive throughout. Coordinates are target-window relative so
# they hold on both macOS SDL and Linux Xvfb.
delay 1500
wait-window "Grace" 15000
# Fixed settle delay rather than wait-converge: Grace's plot canvas repaints
# continuously under a live X display (Xvfb) and never quiets. See grace-startup.
delay 3000
screenshot initial
# Open the File menu from the menubar, then dismiss it without activating an
# item by releasing over a neutral canvas area (Motif drops the menu on a
# release outside its pane).
target-motion 18 10
button 1 press
delay 400
target-motion 18 40
delay 600
screenshot file-menu
assert-image file-menu common-visible.json
assert-image file-menu grace-file-menu.json
target-motion 400 300
button 1 release
delay 400
screenshot dismissed
# Rubber-band drag across the canvas interior (button 1 press, move, release).
target-motion 300 300
button 1 press
delay 200
target-motion 460 460
delay 200
button 1 release
delay 1000
screenshot dragged
assert-image dragged common-visible.json
assert-exit running
